From 0ffb0cdfe7a47b7caa7779dd6cee85658d8202e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:18:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] First visit: the late code in 4 files, loaded one at a
 time when idle

The one late file froze the phone for about 800 ms at 4x CPU when it ran. Now parts-v2.json "late" is 4 groups by page, one file
each (v2-late-1.js to v2-late-4.js): 1 Battle and Test run, 2 Meta, Usage, Sets, Guide, 3 Calc, Types, Practice, Speed, 4 Events,
This Week, Track, Compare, share images.
- split-late.mjs: names shared between late files go through V2.lateReg; a file that uses another's names or V2 names lists it
  as a dependency (checked for loops); the loader runs dependencies first.
- late.js: when idle after today's numbers, one file at a time with a 400 ms gap; each runs in its own task. A late page opened
  early asks for its own file and the ones it needs at once. Held taps wait only for the files they need. fetchPriority high, so
  Home's crowd of sprites doesn't hold the files back.
- Measured: each file's run 210-301 ms (medians), worst 360 ms; the one-file builds are byte-identical (cmp).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YGeTVQdFPaKNkn33jSEpxs
